<title>SOUTH AFRICA: TABLE - Cashbuild lifts year shr, no div.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Cashbuild lifts year shr, no div.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to June 28 vs 53 weeks to June 29, 1996</p>
<p>		 (million of rand unless indicated)</p>
<p>    Shr (cts)		 29.7     vs 13.7</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   6.89     vs 3.19</p>
<p>    Pre-Tax		  12.82     vs 5.34</p>
<p>    Tax			 4.66     vs 2.10</p>
<p>    Finance charges	 7.72     vs 5.12</p>
<p>    Turnover		766.31     vs 689.78</p>
<p>Full name: Cashbuild Ltd (rural-based cash and carry wholesaler)</p>
<p>NOTE: The group said it was achieving real growth for the first time in many years, but could still not declare a dividend because of current high borrowings. The benefits of a computerisation programme, a mass media advertising campaign aimed at rural areas and store remodelling would be felt in the current year, it added.</p>
<p>-- Cape Town newsroom +27 21 25-2238</p>
</text>
